      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "After year 3, the accumulated depreciation would be 3 times the annual depreciation, so that would be $12,500 * 3 = $37,500. To find the book value, subtract the accumulated depreciation from the initial cost of the equipment. Therefore, the book value at the end of year 3 would be $150,000 - $37,500 = $112,500. This figure appears as the new historical cost of the asset on the balance sheet.",
      "source": "target",
